I've just spent some time reading about different types of swords.
From what I understand, the current sword system in nethack is pretty
arbitrary. In reality, there is no clear cut distinction between the
different types of swords. A 'longsword' would usually refer to two-
handed sword; a broadsword could be anything between a short sword and
a great sword (longsword). Scimitars, sabers, and katanas are all
examples of 'backswords'. A knight would likely carry an 'arming
sword', which would be something like a short sword...

So it's all a bit of a mess. It seems to me that the system could
benefit from a good overhaul, but I'll restrain myself for the time
being, mostly because I'm not confident about how best to proceed. I
prefer to move away from the standard game gradually rather than in
great leaps; after all, I do like vanilla nethack.

For now I'll just go ahead with my weapon-skill grouping. To start
with I'll group short sword & broadsword, longsword & two-handed
sword, scimitar & saber. With that, the short sword & broadsword group
will still be quite weak... to help them along I think I'll follow the
path of modders before me =96 add a silver short sword.

In addition to that, I think try some temporary experimental changes:
reduce the weight of short swords from 30 to 25. Replace the starting
longsword of knights and Valkyries with a short sword and a spear
respectively. With that, I think longswords will be slightly less
dominant...


